alty insurance products in the United States. It operates in two segments, Insurance and CenterWell. The Insurance segment offers individual Medicare Advantage products, including health insurance benefits, including wellness programs, chronic care management, and care coordination; individual Medicare stand-alone prescription drug products (PDP); group Medicare advantage and Medicare stand-alone PDP; Medicare supplements; specialty and ancillary insurance comprising dental, vision, life and disability; and administrative services to arrange health care services for active-duty and retired military personnel and dependents, as well as pharmacy benefit managers. Its CenterWell segment operates full-service, value-based senior focused primary care centers under the Conviva Senior Primary Care and CenterWell Senior Primary Care brands; a management services organization; CenterWell Home Health, a home health provider; and OneHome, which manages post-acute patient needs, as well as provides pharmacy and hospice solutions. The company was formerly known as Extendicare Inc. and changed its name to Humana Inc. in April 1974. Humana Inc. was founded in 1961 and is headquartered in Louisville, Kentucky.","ceo_bio":"Mr. James A. Rechtin M.B.A. | President, CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $4.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 67K people. Revenue per employee of $1.9M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $6K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Humana Inc. is a large-cap healthcare business with a $54.0B market cap on $129.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 31% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 23-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $375M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 0 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.78\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 4.3\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.1%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8523012599838665},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $2.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 30% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","15 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Healthcare peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Humana\u2019s chief legal officer trims holding by 20.1% in a stock sale (NYSE: HUM)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/humanas-chief-legal-officer-trims-holding-by-20-1-in-a-stock-sale-nyse-hum.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794528903.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.872,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Do Improved Star Ratings Change The Bull Case For Humana (HUM)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/healthcare/nyse-hum/humana/news/do-improved-star-ratings-change-the-bull-case-for-humana-hum","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794518547.341,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.941,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Wayne A.I. Frederick Disposes of 440 Humana Shares at $440.575 Each","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/wayne-ai-frederick-disposes-of-440-humana-shares-at-440575-each","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794514130.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":1